      "text": "An operating system handles requests to resources as follows. A process (which asks for some resources, uses them for some time and then exits the system) is assigned a unique timestamp are when it starts. The timestamps are monotonically increasing with time. Let us denote the timestamp of a process When a process requests for a resource the does the following: If no other process is currently holding the resource, the awards the resource to If some process is holding the resource, the wait for the resources. If some process is holding the resource, the and awards the resources . (Restarting means taking back the resources held by a process, killing it and starting it again with the same timestamp) When a process releases a resource, the process with the smallest timestamp (if any) amongst those waiting for the resource is awarded the resource.",
